Atkinson Hyperlegible
Version 1.002
Copyright (c) 2020 Braille Institute of America, Inc., a 501(c)(3)
Charitable Organization.

License, quoted from the font files themselves (OpenType name ID 13):

    Braille Institute of America, Inc. provides Atkinson Hyperlegible for
    use, without derivatives or alteration, to the public free of charge
    for all non-commercial and commercial work. No attribution required.

This is the Braille Institute's own license, not the SIL Open Font License.
The distinction matters: later releases of Atkinson Hyperlegible are
published under the OFL via Google Fonts, and the OFL permits modification.
These files, version 1.002, do not. Anyone reusing this repository's
MIT-licensed code should not assume they may alter or subset these fonts.

The build copies both files byte for byte into dist/_astro/fonts/ — no
subsetting or transformation is applied, so what is served is the font as
the Braille Institute published it.
